  "notes": [
    "Ogg Vorbis source decoder for the audio importer (Docs/Design/AudioSystem.ko.md sections 3.10.1 and 3.28). Developer only: AudioTools links it, runtime targets do not.",
    "Vorbis.Build.cs adds the Ogg include directories, because libvorbis includes ogg/ogg.h; the consumer links both Ogg and Vorbis.",
    "The block, psy, envelope and bitrate sources are part of the analysis side but block.c references them from the shared dsp setup, so they are compiled; vorbisenc.c (encoder setup) is not imported.",
    "Decoding is float math without SIMD or runtime CPU dispatch, so decoded samples are fixed per architecture and compiler flags (section 3.10.1).",
    "Consumers define OV_EXCLUDE_STATIC_CALLBACKS (the library's own guard) so that vorbisfile.h does not put the unused stdio callback functions into every including C++ unit; AudioTools uses memory callbacks.",
    "lookup.c is imported but not compiled: with FLOAT_LOOKUP and INT_LOOKUP undefined it produces no definitions.",
    "A Linux tool build would need HAVE_ALLOCA_H (glibc -std=c17 does not declare alloca otherwise) and Vorbis before Ogg in the static link order (GNU ld resolves left to right)."
  ],
